From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] m68k-all: do not race the emu68 Exec backend

arch/m68k-all/exec and arch/m68k-emu68/exec both declare %build_archspecific
for switch, dispatch and preparecontext, and both write to the same object
path -- gen/rom/exec/exec/arch/switch.o. %build_archspecific has no notion of
one overriding another, so this is not an override, it is a race: whichever
rule runs last wins.

We had been winning it by accident. On 2026-08-07 a full rebuild reversed the
order for the first time. The 66-byte objects went into the ELF beside a
kernel_cpu.c that deliberately removes m68k_SwitchTail and m68k_DispatchFrame
as dead code, so the references could not resolve, and the guest jumped to
address zero 570 ms after start -- PC = 0x00000000, five kilobytes of serial
where there are normally thousands of lines.

Emu68's loader had reported it in plain text at load time:

    [ELF] Undefined symbol 'm68k_DispatchFrame' in section '.text'
    [ELF] Undefined symbol 'm68k_SwitchTail' in section '.text'

Zero occurrences of that line in every previous boot log, and nothing was
reading it. scripts/build-aros.sh now fails on an ELF with any unresolved
symbol, because a good one has none.

The fix is to stop offering the files for this target rather than to try to
win the race harder. m68k-amiga needs nothing of the sort: this is the first
m68k target to want a different scheduler, which is why a collision that has
been latent in the build for as long as our backend has existed only surfaced
now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/m68k-all/exec/mmakefile.src | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/m68k-all/exec/mmakefile.src b/arch/m68k-all/exec/mmakefile.src
index 07a85d625a..be38648ec2 100644
--- a/arch/m68k-all/exec/mmakefile.src
+++ b/arch/m68k-all/exec/mmakefile.src
@@ -40,6 +40,27 @@ AFILES=newstackswap stackswap \
        preserveall \
        debug
 
+# The Emu68 port replaces the Exec context backend -- arch/m68k-emu68/exec
+# carries a 68-byte task frame that is self-contained, where the scheme here
+# balances only while entry and exit are paired.
+#
+# Both mmakefiles build into the same object path, and %build_archspecific has
+# no notion of one overriding the other: they race, and whichever rule runs
+# last wins. That is not a theoretical concern. On 2026-08-07 a full rebuild
+# reversed the order for the first time, the 66-byte objects went into the ELF
+# next to a kernel_cpu.c that had deliberately removed m68k_SwitchTail and
+# m68k_DispatchFrame, and the boot jumped to address zero 570 ms in. Emu68's
+# loader had said so plainly -- "Undefined symbol 'm68k_DispatchFrame'" -- and
+# nothing was reading it.
+#
+# So do not offer them at all for this target. m68k-amiga needs no such thing:
+# this is the first m68k target to want a different scheduler, which is why
+# the collision had never surfaced.
+ifeq ($(ARCH),emu68)
+FILES  := $(filter-out preparecontext,$(FILES))
+AFILES := $(filter-out switch dispatch,$(AFILES))
+endif
+
 USER_INCLUDES := $(PRIV_EXEC_INCLUDES)
 USER_AFLAGS := -I$(GENINCDIR)
 TARGET_ISA_AFLAGS:=$(ISA_MC68060_FLAGS)
